+# Two analytic requirements collide at K=27 (docs/band_geometry_theory.md 6.5):
+#   Requirement N (signal): the c^2-weighted training mass must not be dominated
+#     by states whose Bayes posterior is uninformative. W = irreducible share.
+#   Requirement S (support): the sampler starts at x0, i.e. gamma=0. If
+#     gamma_lo > 0 that init is OUTSIDE the trained band, by kappa = t_lo/sqrt(K-1)
+#     noise radii. Their feasible sets do not intersect below K ~ 1024, so which
+#     one binds is an EMPIRICAL question. This ladder measures it.
